===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|hord}}, from {{inh|en|ang|hord|t=an accumulation of valuable objects cached for preservation or future use; treasure; hoard}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*hoʀd}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*huzdą|t=treasure; hoard}}, of unknown origin, but possibly derived from {{der|en|ine-pro|*(s)kewH-|*kewdʰ-|to conceal, hide}}, thus meaning “something hidden”.<ref>{{R:gem:EDPG|*huzda-|260}}</ref> Cognate with {{cog|de|Hort|t=hoard; refuge}}, {{cog|is|hodd|t=treasure}}, {{cog|la|cū̆stōs|t=guard; keeper}}. For the meaning development compare {{m+|ru|сокро́вище||treasure}} related to {{m+|ru|скрыва́ть||to hide, to conceal}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[hidden]] [[supply]] or [[fund]].
#: {{ux|en|a '''hoard''' of provisions; a '''hoard''' of money}}
# {{lb|en|archaeology}} A [[cache]] of [[valuable]] objects or [[artefact]]s; a [[trove]].

